id: pm-3z0k
title: "Portable integrity attestation: export a detached hash-chain proof bundle and verify it standalone, so third parties can confirm the recorded history was never altered"
description: Export and independently verify detached hash-chain proof bundles so third parties can attest tracker history integrity without the original workspace.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: governance,history,immutable-record
created_at: "2026-07-06T23:19:12.124Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-10T19:29:42.668Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-10T19:09:57.765Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-10T19:09:57.765Z"
author: maintainer-agent
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "attest export produces a documented, versioned bundle covering all item and workspace history streams with a workspace rollup digest; verify against a bundle detects any post-export stream rewrite and names the diverged streams; verify runs read-only with no locks and works on a bare clone; compact/redact/repair produce lineage-visible digest transitions (tested); SDK exposes export/verify primitives with reference docs; bundle stays small (KBs, independent of workspace size beyond stream count)"
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: low
confidence: medium
resolution: "Added versioned exact-byte per-stream commitments and deterministic workspace rollups, strict proof parsing, complete stream comparison and maintenance transitions; thin history attest transport exports exclusive proof files or complete stdout artifacts."
expected_result: "Export every retained item/workspace stream, verify bare history copies without writes or hooks, identify all divergences and intentional maintenance, and expose documented extensible SDK primitives."
actual_result: Packed npm/npx and Bun/bunx manual acceptance passed; SDK and real Commander linked tests passed; a 2746-stream repository proof matched successful backend telemetry; all 8697 tests passed with zero uncovered source counts; missing or malformed proof files and existing outputs now yield actionable usage errors.
